WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.422
Pandas mainly gives us two important structures.

00:00:03.422 --> 00:00:09.497
A Series represents one labeled dimension, which you can think of as one column.

00:00:09.497 --> 00:00:15.197
A DataFrame represents a full table with rows and multiple named columns.

00:00:15.197 --> 00:00:20.952
If we select one column, such as amount, Pandas often returns a Series.

00:00:20.952 --> 00:00:25.867
If we select several columns, Pandas returns another DataFrame.

00:00:25.867 --> 00:00:32.457
This distinction matters because some methods behave differently depending on the object you are working with.

00:00:32.457 --> 00:00:37.977
A useful beginner habit is to ask, what object do I have right now?

00:00:37.977 --> 00:00:40.867
Is it a Series or a DataFrame?

00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:45.654
Many confusing errors become easier to understand once you know the answer.
